query:
AITA for keeping my roommate up watching a movie okay so under just normal circumstances YTA would be a straight forward no-brainer, but hear me out.

(we live in a dorm, at uni,  in close enough proximity to each other to be able to see each other)

&#x200B;

so I don't usually sleep a lot (I go to bed late and get up early), but I was extra tired so I went to bed at about 9:00 P.M.  It didn't take me long to fall asleep even though my roommate was playing on his console. Anyways, he constantly keeps waking me up: turning lights on and off, yelling at people in chat, and slamming shit when he gets pissed he dies. I'm sleeping intermittently, and he finally decides it time to go to sleep somewhere around 12-12:30 A.M. he's super loud and wakes me up as he's getting ready for bed/doing random shit (if I purposefully kept him up bc of this tho...major YTA. because usually I'm not in the room at this time and normally awake if i am).

&#x200B;

So now I'm awake

&#x200B;

I mostly just lay in my bed trying to go back to sleep as he passes out, and can't. so i get bored around 1:30 and start fucking around on reddit, and eventually see a post that reminds me of the dc aquaman movie that i still hadn't seen at about 3 A.M.  So i decide to watch aquaman, and look over at my desk to get my earbuds.

&#x200B;

but my earbuds aren't there.........

&#x200B;

I must have left them in my car. My roommate is dead asleep by this point, and he usually doesn't wake up super easy. so i figure playing it out loud is fine as long as it's quiet enough that it doesn't wake him up. I don't see him move at all, and didn't figure he woke up. So 5 A.M. rolls around and his alarm goes off. He gets up, gets ready for PT, and makes a rude comment about me watching a movie since 3.

&#x200B;

The comment didn't really bother me because iv'e told him plenty of times to tell me if I'm doing anything that's getting on his nerves/keeping him from doing shit he needs to do. mostly I'm just confused as to why he didn't tell me to shut the hell up when I woke him up instead of waiting ~~3~~ 2 hours.

&#x200B;

Edit: sorry I can't do math apparently.

AITA for telling my own mother to shut up? Before you instantly downvote/say that ITA (which I'm expecting at this point), hear me out. For some background, I'm currently enrolled in a summer course to regain credits that I need to proceed to grade/year 10 in school.

&#x200B;

I was in the car with my mom, and we were driving home. I was talking to her about how the classes went, and she was talking about work. We then got on the topic on bills, which I help her submit payments through her bank for, and how I never paid a specific bill. Obviously, the bill was late, and she was charged a late fee. At that point, I felt really bad because it was my fault that this was happening, but then she starts saying how her bills are more important than my computer, which she says all the time, and I understand what the point she was trying to get through was.

However, I got frustrated with how she was constantly reminding me that it's my fault that she was charged, and I raised my voice at her. I told her that if she didn't trust me with her bills, she can either have my brother do them, or I could show her how to submit the payments. Then, she said "You know what? I don't deserve to get yelled at like this. Watch what'll happen when I don't call you to wake you up for school. Maybe you'll stay in the 9th grade for the rest of your life."

At this point, I lost it. I yelled at her (still in the car) "SHUT UP! I DON'T WANT A CONSTANT REMINDER ON HOW MUCH OF A FUCKUP I AM!" and got out of the car. At this point, we had parked in front of our house. And I then said "I hate how you keep reminding me of my failures, it's so fucking annoying" and unlocked the door. Upon entering the house, I ran to my room, and shut the door. And now I'm here, writing the post.

&#x200B;

So r/AmItheAsshole, am I the asshole in this? Because right now, I feel like a total piece of shit for yelling at the person who gave birth to me.

&#x200B;

Edit: I don't think I was clear about the "I help pay for my mom's bills" part. I send in the payments for her bills, but she's the one who's giving the money to pay for the actual bills.
